  "style": {
    "name": "heroic-cartoon figurative",
    "rationale": "A freestanding dancing man read through pose, not anatomy: planted center leg over a 6x6 terracotta plinth that catches the center of mass so the opposite leg can high-kick out to -x as a cantilever, while the arms fling asymmetrically (right up, left out) to draw a jagged diagonal silhouette that differs from every side. Warm analogous palette builds the body in the round — terracotta skin/head, red_terracotta shirt with jagged shoulder pads, brown_terracotta trousers/legs, an orange_terracotta waist belt where shirt meets trousers — and the single cool-bright gold_block accent crowns the motion as hat, hands, and shoes. All masses are full-depth solids (z spanning both sides) so the object reads as volume from front, back, and either flank; the hidden far side mirrors the visible torso/head volumes for a finished surface all the way around."
  },
